# A copy of a spell has the text spliced onto it (CR 702.47c, 707.10), and the new targets it may have (CR 707.10c) include
# those of the spliced text, in the slots after the spell's own: Bot1 casts Hex Magic (an Arcane spell with no target)
# with Goryo's Vengeance spliced on, aimed at Yargle, Glutton of Urborg in its graveyard, and Lutri, the Spellchaser copies
# it. The copy's spliced target is asked again and becomes Yargle, Goliath of Otaria. The copy returns Goliath, the original
# Glutton: both legends are on the battlefield with haste.

